% Test cases for the lower limb prosthesis policy (lower_limb_prostheses.le):
% synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33787 and per payment
% condition of Policy Article A52496, each stating only what its record
% shows. The functional level is the number the clinical assessment
% designates (K0–K4 as 0–4); a component is an accessory of its prosthesis.
% The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query, so "stage"
% reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and what
% minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base lower_limb_prostheses cases includes these resources:
    lower_limb_prostheses.

the knowledge base lower_limb_prostheses cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a microprocessor knee (L5856, on the prior
% authorization list) on an endoskeletal above knee prosthesis (L5321) for a
% community ambulator (level 3): the findings, the prosthetist's records
% supporting the level, the functional need for the knee's feature, the
% prior authorization, the order and the delivery.
scenario microprocessor_knee_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the microprocessor knee.
    the HCPCS code of the microprocessor knee is "L5856".
    the microprocessor knee is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the microprocessor knee is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis is "L5321".
    the prosthesis is furnished to Ann.
    the functional level of Ann is 3, according to the prosthetist.
    the finding functional state reachable about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the records of the prosthetist support the functional level designated for Ann.
    the records document the functional need for the design feature of the microprocessor knee.
    the order for the microprocessor knee is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the microprocessor knee is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes order date.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes description of the item.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the microprocessor knee was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    prior authorization for the microprocessor knee was affirmed on 2026-03-01.
    the microprocessor knee was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the microprocessor knee.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The same claim without the documentation of the functional need for the
% microprocessor feature: reasonable and necessary, not payable.
scenario knee_feature_undocumented is:
    claim 1 is for the microprocessor knee.
    the HCPCS code of the microprocessor knee is "L5856".
    the microprocessor knee is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the microprocessor knee is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis is "L5321".
    the prosthesis is furnished to Ann.
    the functional level of Ann is 3, according to the prosthetist.
    the finding functional state reachable about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the records of the prosthetist support the functional level designated for Ann.
    the order for the microprocessor knee is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the microprocessor knee is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes order date.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes description of the item.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the microprocessor knee includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the microprocessor knee was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    prior authorization for the microprocessor knee was affirmed on 2026-03-01.
    the microprocessor knee was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the microprocessor knee.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the records document the functional need for the design feature of the microprocessor knee"]].

% A below knee prosthesis (L5301) for a beneficiary of potential functional
% level 0: never reasonable and necessary.
scenario level_zero is:
    claim 1 is for the prosthesis.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis is "L5301".
    the prosthesis is furnished to Ben.
    the functional level of Ben is 0, according to the prosthetist.
    the finding functional state reachable about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A household ambulator (level 1): the prosthesis (claim 1), an external
% keel SACH foot (level 1, claim 2) and another knee system (level 1,
% claim 4) are covered; a flexible-keel foot (level 2, claim 3) is not.
scenario household_ambulator is:
    claim 1 is for the prosthesis.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis is "L5321".
    the prosthesis is furnished to Cy.
    claim 2 is for the SACH foot.
    the HCPCS code of the SACH foot is "L5970".
    the SACH foot is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the SACH foot is furnished to Cy.
    claim 3 is for the flexible keel foot.
    the HCPCS code of the flexible keel foot is "L5972".
    the flexible keel foot is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the flexible keel foot is furnished to Cy.
    claim 4 is for the knee.
    the HCPCS code of the knee is "L5611".
    the knee is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the knee is furnished to Cy.
    the functional level of Cy is 1, according to the prosthetist.
    the finding functional state reachable about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Microprocessor knees at level 2: one indicated for level 2 with stumble
% recovery, for a beneficiary who can charge it and respond to its alerts
% (claim 1); one without stumble recovery (claim 2).
scenario microprocessor_knee_level_two is:
    claim 1 is for the stance knee.
    the HCPCS code of the stance knee is "L5858".
    the stance knee is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the stance knee is furnished to Dee.
    the stance knee is indicated for functional level 2.
    the stance knee detects a stumble of the user and stabilizes the knee unit.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis is "L5321".
    the prosthesis is furnished to Dee.
    the functional level of Dee is 2, according to the prosthetist.
    Dee had a clinical evaluation to determine the functional level.
    the finding functional state reachable about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding advanced knee system justified about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "fewer falls, safe descent of the stairs at home; a mechanical knee buckled twice in therapy".
    Dee is able to make use of a product that requires daily charging.
    Dee is able to understand and respond to error alerts of the unit.
    claim 2 is for the swing knee.
    the HCPCS code of the swing knee is "L5857".
    the swing knee is an accessory of the other prosthesis.
    the swing knee is furnished to Eve.
    the swing knee is indicated for functional level 2.
    the HCPCS code of the other prosthesis is "L5321".
    the other prosthesis is furnished to Eve.
    the functional level of Eve is 2, according to the prosthetist.
    Eve had a clinical evaluation to determine the functional level.
    the finding functional state reachable about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding advanced knee system justified about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    Eve is able to make use of a product that requires daily charging.
    Eve is able to understand and respond to error alerts of the unit.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A level 3 energy storing foot (L5976) at level 2 with a pneumatic knee
% (L5613) covered at level 2: covered when the foot is required for the
% safe use of the knee.
scenario level_three_foot_at_level_two is:
    claim 1 is for the energy storing foot.
    the HCPCS code of the energy storing foot is "L5976".
    the energy storing foot is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the energy storing foot is furnished to Fay.
    claim 2 is for the pneumatic knee.
    the HCPCS code of the pneumatic knee is "L5613".
    the pneumatic knee is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the pneumatic knee is furnished to Fay.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis is "L5321".
    the prosthesis is furnished to Fay.
    the functional level of Fay is 2, according to the prosthetist.
    Fay had a clinical evaluation to determine the functional level.
    the finding functional state reachable about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding advanced knee system justified about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding higher level foot required about Fay is established, according to the prosthetist.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Components never covered: a flex foot (L5980) on a preparatory below knee
% prosthesis (L5510), the powered ankle addition (L5969); the donning
% sleeve (L7600) is in no benefit. The preparatory prosthesis itself is
% covered (claim 4).
scenario never_covered is:
    claim 1 is for the flex foot.
    the HCPCS code of the flex foot is "L5980".
    the flex foot is an accessory of the preparatory prosthesis.
    the flex foot is furnished to Gus.
    claim 2 is for the power ankle.
    the HCPCS code of the power ankle is "L5969".
    the power ankle is an accessory of the preparatory prosthesis.
    the power ankle is furnished to Gus.
    claim 3 is for the donning sleeve.
    the HCPCS code of the donning sleeve is "L7600".
    the donning sleeve is an accessory of the preparatory prosthesis.
    the donning sleeve is furnished to Gus.
    claim 4 is for the preparatory prosthesis.
    the HCPCS code of the preparatory prosthesis is "L5510".
    the preparatory prosthesis is furnished to Gus.
    the functional level of Gus is 3, according to the prosthetist.
    the finding functional state reachable about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The Council finds the record does not show the beneficiary motivated to
% ambulate: the prosthesis, and so its knee, are not reasonable and
% necessary.
scenario council_motivation_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the prosthesis.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthesis is "L5321".
    the prosthesis is furnished to Hal.
    claim 2 is for the knee.
    the HCPCS code of the knee is "L5611".
    the knee is an accessory of the prosthesis.
    the knee is furnished to Hal.
    the functional level of Hal is 1, according to the prosthetist.
    the finding functional state reachable about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding motivated to ambulate about Hal is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the notes record that the beneficiary declined gait training and uses a wheelchair for all transfers".
    rn expects answers [].
